1. Download Raspberry Pi Imager in official Raspberry Pi website
2. Connect SD card to laptop using Micro SD card reader. Memory should be minimum 32 gigabytes
3. Open Raspberry Pi Imager
4. Select Raspberry Pi 5 in Device
5. Select Raspberry Pi OS 64 bit in OS
6. Select Generic MassStorageClass USB Drive as storage
7. Choose hostname (raspberrypi)
8. Select time zone and keyboard layout
10. Create username and password (username: pi, password: raspberrypi)
11. Enter wifi credentials
12. Enable SSH
13. Disable Raspberry Pi Connect
14. Write the data, it's okay if the data on the sd card is erased
